## Safety (always on)
- Never read, print or commit `.env`, keys or tokens. Never force-push, delete remote branches, `git reset --hard`, `git clean -f`, `rm -rf`, `sudo`, or use `--no-verify`.
- Merging to `main`, deleting files/branches, and changing visibility need the owner's explicit approval; open a PR and stop.
- Enforcement: `bash hooks/install.sh` (git hooks: commit-msg, pre-commit, pre-push) + `.codex/hooks.json` / `.agents/hooks.json` (tool hooks) + `.codex/rules/studio.rules`.
  Trust the project `.codex/` layer and review hooks in Codex with `/hooks`; in AGY check `.agents/hooks.json` under Settings > Customizations > Hooks.
- Session start (optional, for a status brief): `bash .claude/hooks/session-start.sh`. New project with no engine/concept: run the `start` skill.

